title: Gnomon first dogfood path complete on macOS; Mac daily-driver lanes underway
summary: |-
  On 2026-10-18 these all landed on feat/gnomon (green x8 at fa100167), each through reviewer + Aegis:
  - M1.3 slice 1 (Secure Enclave helper, identity init/rotate/recover)
  - gnomon up (real-home in-process launcher, unsafe-env refusal)
  - P8-D96 permission channel (--permission-prompts host + stdio; Edit/Write/Bash cards with Touch ID; ask rules; ungated-tool-use detector)
  - M1.7 s2 (session read-deny, P8-D94 audited repo hooks)
  - T-020 (web child has no network; kernel-accept handoff)
  - T-016 (P8-D93 clientNonce)
  - M1.6 s2, M1.8 s2, M1.12 s3
  The founder ruled P8-D94 (audited repo hooks), P8-D95 (ratifications) and P8-D97 (repo context loads normally). Then the founder set the goal of a Mac daily driver. Five lanes are in flight: the GUI completeness pass (ask-user picker, always rules), the M1.13 signed Tauri app, security hardening (SIGUSR1, unlock TTL, helper exec deny), M1.11 s3 (gnomon mod CLI + Workshop), and the repo context (stripped plugin-dir + add-dir).
