learnings:
  - Builder stalls (turn limits, waiting on background work) cost more wall-clock than CI; heartbeat checks every 15 min plus commit-per-item briefs fixed most of it
  - 'Windows/Linux CI traps recur: keys/ dir modes, world-writable /tmp homes, POSIX path fixtures, '':'' in names, JSON-escaped paths'
  - Real-Claude probes before building (p01b, p10m-repo-surfaces, p10m-repo-context) caught design-breaking assumptions early
